# Story 78: Routing Agent Output (40s)
# Hook: Send a headless agent's replies straight into a pane you can watch.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-078-routing-agent-output.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Send a headless agent's replies straight into a pane you can watch.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh and give this pane a name with ##pane name -- that's where we'll route the agent's output.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
Spawn an agent. Normally its output stays in the background -- it has no pane of its own.

[00:16.0 --> 00:26.0]
Register its output to a pane and every reply lands in that pane's chat buffer -- a live feed of the agent's work.

[00:26.0 --> 00:34.0]
When you're done watching, ##agent unregister-output stops the routing. The agent keeps running -- you just stop tailing it here.

[00:34.0 --> 00:40.0]
register-output turns any pane into a dashboard for your background agents.

